-    <p>Cluster-robust sandwich estimator for meta-regression with dependent effect sizes (multiple outcomes per study, multi-arm trials, repeated measures). Implements the Hedges-Tipton-Johnson 2010 correlated-effects (CORR) working model with a CR1 small-sample correction. The robustness is to <em>misspecification of the within-cluster correlation ρ</em> — it closes the inverse-variance underestimate that breaks fixed-effect / standard random-effects meta-regression when effects are nested. Coverage is good when the number of clusters is reasonably large; with <strong>few clusters (m≲20) the CR1 SEs are anticonservative</strong> — see the footer and use <code>robumeta</code>/<code>clubSandwich</code> (CR2) in R for inference there.</p>
